  "scope": "Complete Dominican Canon constituent as the 1553 book prints it: from fol. 89r (canvas 219) Te igitur under the woodcut through fol. 90r (canvas 221) omnis honor, et gloria, left column, immediately followed by the notated Per omnia secula seculorum under the page's red running head Cantus solennis (this book prints no in-column heading there). 14 source-order units, 26 printed crosses, no rubrics printed within these bounds. The book sets the concluding Per omnia saecula saeculorum. Amen only in the following notated chant block, which is excluded with it. Whole-book and complete-Ordinary coverage remain partial; no wording is inherited from another edition.",
